            <ArticleTitle>Sinonasal Schwannoma: A Rare Sinonasal Neoplasm.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>425-427</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1007/s12070-017-1125-2</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Neoplasm in sinonasal cavity is dominated by epithelial type. Sinonasal schwannoma is a rare entity represent less than four percent of head and neck schwannoma. Clinically this tumour is commonly misdiagnosed until they are confirmed by histopathological examination. We present a case of schwannoma in sinonasal region with involvement of right side nasal cavity, maxillary sinus and maxillary alveolar process. The tumour was successfully removed by midfacial degloving approach.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
